@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Research Engine — Phase 7: Unrationed output, public documentation, the semantic tier, enforcement, consolidation (10-10-2026)
+
+**Source:** the Research Engine audit (`RESEARCH-ENGINE-AUDIT-2026-10-08.md`): §F ①b (a semantic matcher over a synonym lexicon for low-confidence intents), §F ⑤ and §E "Validation" (research-level checks as blockers), §C.2 #1/#4 and §K Phase 1's output discipline (the answer must be complete, not cheap), and the consolidation pass the roadmap closes with — the whole of Phases 1–6 re-read against the code. Two asks from the brief that the audit did not list are here too: Intelligent mode **does not ration tokens** — the correct, complete answer is what matters — and ReScript Studio is **publicly documented** for the AI tools (ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity, Google's) that a researcher will ask "how do I program this in ReScript Studio?", as Qualtrics and Decipher are. Every change has a regression test and the tests were mutation-checked. Nothing existing was removed; the semantic tier runs only where the recognisers had nothing, the blockers only when the design is enforced, the docs are read-only public pages.
+
+## Checklist
+
+| ID | Finding | Change | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| T1 | Output was rationed: `maxTokens` 8000 for generation, 2500 for an edit, 3 continuations; a long questionnaire was cut off and the researcher told to ask for less | `apps/studio/lib/copilot/budget.ts`: `outputBudget(kind)` — the **provider's ceiling** (`AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`, default 32 000, never below 8 000) is what every call may use, the **expected size** per kind is what the meter reserves, **8 continuations**, a timeout per kind. Every copilot call (turn, plan, item, repair, coverage, narrative, document summary, workflow) asks for the ceiling. `packages/ai`: a provider's 400 "max_tokens too large" is read (`outputCeilingFrom`), the ceiling remembered per endpoint+model and the call retried once at it — a Studio configured above what the provider allows still gets its full answer. The truncated failure says the ceiling is the provider's, names `AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` and *Plan first* | ✅ |
+| T2 | No public documentation; an AI tool asked about ReScript Studio has nothing to read | `apps/studio/content/docs/*.md` — fourteen pages (≈1 600 lines): the definition, question types, logic in text and JSON, the logic reference, piping and lists, custom code (per-question HTML/CSS/JS, survey scripts and their API, the UX layer, branding code), Intelligent mode with a catalogue of **110 sentences and what the engine reads them as**, the actions reference, the research engine, data and exports, localization and quotas, the HTTP API. Three pages are **generated from the code** (`scripts/gen-public-docs.mjs`, `--check` in the tests) so they cannot drift. Served at `/docs` and `/docs/<slug>` (a dependency-free, fully-escaping markdown renderer), as raw markdown at `/docs/<slug>.md`, as `llms.txt` and `llms-full.txt` for AI crawlers, with `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` (absolute only with `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`); all public in the middleware and listed in the auth-guard audit | ✅ |
+| T3 | §F ①b: a sentence outside the recognisers' forms went to the model even when it meant a plain edit | `packages/engine/src/nlSemanticMatch.ts`: `stripPreamble` (politeness, "I'd like you to", "can we"), a **lexicon of 19 intents** with cue phrases and strengths (required/optional, delete, randomize, own page, move, duplicate, terminate, show/hide if, add/remove option, crosstab, test, what depends, objective, hypothesis, measure), **fuzzy object resolution** (code, variable, wording with every word family present, typo distance, population phrases, conditions in words), each candidate rewritten as a **canonical sentence** the recognisers already read and verified by reading it. `interpretRequest` uses it only where a recogniser handed the sentence to the model or refused a missing object: a clear reading (score ≥ 0.7 with a margin, or a lone ≥ 0.5) is proposed as "Read “…” as “…”"; a close call is a **clarification with the readings as choices**; a bare object ("Q7") offers what can be done with it | ✅ |
+| T4 | §F ⑤: research-level checks were warnings; a change could silently leave a hypothesis unmeasured | `research.strict` on the design (schema), the `rd-strict` switch in the editor and the sentences *enforce / stop enforcing the research design* (`set_research {strict}`). `researchBlockers(def)`: unmeasured construct, unlinked or unmeasured hypothesis, dead plan reference, dead derived variable, dead KPI, empty design. When enforced, **a batch that opens a gap is refused** in `applySurveyActions` with the gap and the fix named (each result carries the line; the engine's dry-run shows it in Changes before anything is applied), and the review marks the gaps `blocks` first (`cp-review-blockers`). Turning enforcement on with gaps present is allowed — that is how they become visible | ✅ |
+| C1 | Consolidation — question-scoped `on_validate`/`on_submit` scripts and page-scoped `on_change` scripts **never ran**: `runScripts` matched one id and the runner passed the page id on submit and the question id on change | `runScripts` takes the **set** of ids an event belongs to (`scopeRef: string \| string[]`); the runner and the QA simulator pass the page and every question on it at submit, the question and its page at change; the simulator now runs `on_validate` before `on_submit` as the runner does. Documented in custom-code | ✅ fixed |
+| C2 | Consolidation — "Review the entire survey and identify problems with the logic" (§F) went to the model as "does not parse that phrasing" while the Review button beside it did exactly this | a `reviewRequest` recogniser: the engine's review as an **answer**, grouped by severity, narrowed to the area named (logic, wording, translations, scales, quotas, …); the Studio fills the Review tab from the same sentence and, with a model in cloud mode, asks for its reading as the button does | ✅ |
+| C3 | Consolidation — §F "Which demographic groups are most likely to prefer Brand A?" and "Create a report showing the key findings" still went to the model | an adjective before *groups* in the data-question grammar; *a report showing / of / on / with the (key) findings* as the findings report | ✅ |
+| C4 | Consolidation — §C.2 #4: the turn cache key was system ∥ prompt ∥ maxTokens; a copy of a survey under another project could be served another project's reply | the key names the project and the person | ✅ |
+| C5 | Consolidation — question `customCss` is unscoped (documented so, with the card's `[data-qid]` hook); `customJs`/`branding.customJs` run unsandboxed (documented: the survey's author is trusted); no API keys or webhooks (documented) | documented, not changed: scoping CSS by rewriting selectors would alter surveys that rely on page-wide rules | ✅ documented |
+| C6 | Consolidation — the audit's §F table re-run against the engine after Phases 1–7 | 25 sentences: 20 read by the engine (actions, answer, query, output), 5 the model's with the engine's own alternative offered on every one (research design → record the objective; measure purchase intent → a standard item; create the questionnaire from the hypothesis; adapt for an audience → record the audience + remove the unconnected; "review" now the engine's). No sentence ends in "not understood" | ✅ |
+
+## What was built
+
+**The budget (`apps/studio/lib/copilot/budget.ts`)** — `BudgetKind` = edit, review, ux, generate, plan, item, repair, coverage, narrative, summary. `maxOutputTokens(env)` reads `AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` (bad → 32 000; floor 8 000; cap 1 000 000). `outputBudget(kind)` = `{ maxTokens: max(ceiling, expected[kind]), expectedTokens, continuations: 8, timeoutMs }`. The meter reserves the expected size (`meteredAi … maxTokens: expectedTokens`) so a wallet is not drained by a reservation it will not use; the call itself may use the ceiling. In `packages/ai`, `completeJson` keeps the known ceiling per `${base} ${model}` (`OUTPUT_CEILING`, `resetOutputCeilings()` for tests); a 400 that names a smaller limit lowers the call once and remembers it; a truncated answer after every continuation reports the limit it hit.
+
+**The docs (`apps/studio/content/docs`, `lib/docs/markdown.ts`, `lib/docs/pages.ts`)** — `DOC_ORDER` is the navigation and `llms.txt`; `readDoc(slug)` accepts one path segment of `[a-z0-9-]`; `renderMarkdown` escapes every character and draws headings (with ids), paragraphs, fences, tables (escaped pipes), lists, quotes, rules; comments are dropped. Routes: `app/docs/page.tsx`, `app/docs/[slug]/page.tsx` (`DocShell` with `docs`, `docs-nav`, `docs-main`), `app/api/docs/[slug]/route.ts` (text/markdown, reached by the middleware rewrite of `/docs/<slug>.md`), `app/llms.txt`, `app/llms-full.txt`, `app/robots.ts`, `app/sitemap.ts`. `next.config.mjs` traces `content/docs` into the deploy. The generator (`scripts/lib/publicDocs.mjs`) builds question-types from the variant registry, logic-reference from the operator, function, piping and UX-API tables in the source, actions-reference from the action union.
+
+**The semantic tier (`packages/engine/src/nlSemanticMatch.ts`)** — `semanticReading(def, text, ctx)` → `{ core, candidates, objects }`; a candidate is `{ intent, canonical, score, why }`. Slots: a question (`fuzzyQuestion`), a pair (split at the cue), a condition (`conditionInWords`: *under 25*, *at least 3*, *N or older*, *is not*, *said X to Q*, and/or), an option (quoted or *a X option*), a concept (only one the standard-measure library knows), a quoted text. `interpretRequest`'s `semantic(r)` verifies up to six candidates by reading each canonical at depth 1 and keeps those that produce actions, answers, queries or a no-op refusal; a model-with-fallback is kept as what the engine can offer.
+
+**Blockers (`packages/engine/src/researchBlockers.ts`)** — `researchStrict(def)`, `researchBlockers(def)`, `newResearchBlockers(before, after)` (the codes present after and not before, so pre-existing gaps do not block unrelated edits). `applySurveyActions` refuses after the schema parse; `reviewSurvey` sets `blocks` and `blockers`; `set_research` carries `strict`; the editor's `rd-strict-box` patches it.
+
+**Script scope (`packages/engine/src/scripts.ts`)** — `refs` is the set; a survey-scoped script runs on every occurrence; `only: "scoped"` still leaves the survey-wide `on_load` to the session open.
+
+## Tests
+
+| Suite | What it checks | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `packages/ai/src/ceiling.test.ts` | a 400 naming a smaller limit lowers the call once and is remembered; a 400 that names nothing is an error; the remembered ceiling never raises a smaller ask | 3 tests |
+| `apps/studio/lib/copilot/budget.test.ts` | the ceiling from the environment (bad, zero, below the floor, above the cap), the expected size per kind, the ceiling never below the expected | 2 tests |
+| `packages/engine/src/nlSemanticMatch.test.ts` | preamble stripping; the lexicon's readings (required, terminate under 25, hide if, add/remove option, move, crosstab) each verified as the canonical's actions; close calls as choices; a bare object's choices; typos; populations and conditions in words; "Exclude the price question" not a terminate | 4 tests |
+| `packages/engine/src/researchBlockers.test.ts` | each blocker code; enforcement refuses the batch that opens a gap and names it, lets a clean batch through, lets enforcement be turned on over gaps; review marks blockers first | 4 tests |
+| `packages/engine/src/publicDocs.test.ts` | the generated pages are current (`--check`); every catalogue row reads as stated against the brand tracker; every logic fence parses; every JSON example validates | 3 tests |
+| `apps/studio/lib/docs/markdown.test.ts` | every construct, everything escaped, comments dropped, first H1 the title; every page in the order exists and renders; a bad slug (traversal, two segments, an extension) is null; llms.txt lists every page; every relative link resolves | 3 tests |
+| `packages/engine/src/scriptScope.test.ts` | a submit runs the page's, its questions' and the survey's scripts, not another question's; `on_validate` fires for a question on the page; a change runs the page's `on_change`; a single id and an empty set behave | 2 tests |
+| `packages/engine/src/consolidation7.test.ts` | the review sentence (area, grouping, the survey's real finding), "check the questionnaire", "what is wrong with the wording", an edit beginning with *check* left alone; "demographic groups"; "a report showing / of the results for the board" | 2 tests |
+| `scripts/phase7-engine-docs-test.mjs` (browser) | the docs without a session (HTML, `.md`, llms.txt, robots, sitemap; the app shell not served); the semantic tier's cards and choices in the sandbox; enforcement end to end (refused in Changes, counted and marked in Review, relaxed in Settings); the review sentence as the engine's card with the Review tab filled | 4 checks |
+
+Totals: engine 1768, ai 36, analytics 253, templates 98, studio 291 unit tests pass; `scripts/auth-guard-audit.mjs` 0 problems; `pnpm -r test` green; `node scripts/gen-public-docs.mjs --check` current.
+
+Mutation checks (`mut_any.py`, each mutation built and run against the whole suite of its package): **engine 17 mutations, all caught** — script scope (the first id only; the set truncated), the semantic tier (always clear; never clear; `unless` ignored; a partial concept accepted; the preamble kept; the rescue off), the blockers (the gate off; the review not marking an existing finding; the review ignoring `strict`; the dead KPI dropped; the review's duplicate line kept), the consolidation recognisers (the adjective before *groups* dropped; *report of* dropped; the review's area ignored; the recogniser removed). Two survived the first run — the review not marking an existing finding, and the area filter — and were caught after the tests were strengthened (a dead plan reference the review already names, now marked once and not added twice; a wording finding that a logic review must leave out). **ai 4/4** (the ceiling never lowered; not remembered; the asked size not excluded; a remembered ceiling raising a smaller ask). **Studio 8/8** (the budget's expected-only, unclamped and zero cases; the renderer's escaping, comments and title; the slug's one segment; a page in the order not on disk — caught after the test was strengthened). The Studio's wiring of the review sentence: 1 mutation, caught by the browser suite (the Review tab not filled).
+
+Browser corpus (135 suites, the new one included): 124 pass; the 10 known baseline failures (ai-conversation, auth-collaboration, billing, dashboard-outage, listfill-allocation, lock-concurrency, picker-taxonomy, qa-fixes, quality, version-scoped-export — the same set as at Phases 1–6, none touched by this phase); blocker-fixes was killed for memory while building its own production Studio beside the dev servers and passes alone (24/24).
+
+## Configuration
+
+`AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` — the provider's output ceiling (default 32 000). `AI_MODEL_SMALL` — the small tier. `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` — makes `robots.txt` point at the sitemap and `llms.txt` carry absolute links. All three documented in `.env.example`.
+
+## Status of the roadmap after this phase
+
+Phases 1–7 of the audit's §K are implemented and verified. The §D "critical" and "high" rows are all closed; of the "medium" rows, derived variables in the compute path, the clean dataset for automatic runs, post-hoc corrections, factor scores, chart selection by purpose, the premium deck, output routing and the model tiers are done; "findings synthesis beyond the plan" (segment discovery, anomalies, wave trends) is done. Of the "low" rows, the research ontology exists as the standard-measure library (purchase intent, satisfaction, likelihood to recommend, awareness, importance, loyalty, trust, usage frequency, price perception) the engine uses without a model; cross-project memory and a project "brief" entity are not built, and the §J architecture remains conceptual as the audit intended.
